  "diary": "The day was a study in the friction between the sign and the Notion. The air in Lodhi Gardens was clear, yet my head remained clouded by a register that has made a dead professor into a Joint Secretary. I walked three kilometres to let the contradiction cool, buying chai from Sunil, who wisely noted that the steam will get into the head before the tea does. The misdescription is not merely a slip of ink; it is an institutional fact that the state’s own machinery now recognizes. I reviewed the vouchers at four, separating the state’s imprest from my own cash, only to find a further discrepancy. My ledger records the dhobi’s bill at three hundred rupees on Saturday; Ramesh claims it is two hundred on Thursday. I refused to let household memory settle state accounts. I demanded the name and address: Salim, of Tughlakabad. The contradiction is now parked in a written note, a tangible obstacle for Monday’s ten o’clock. At dinner, I insisted Ramesh sit. It is a small act of ethics, to refuse the hierarchy of the servant standing while the master sits. The house is quiet now. The file waits. The Notion rests, but it has not been resolved. It has merely been carried into the night, waiting for the light of the next day to expose its internal tension.",
  "revision_log": "The thesis that the state is the actuality of the ethical idea remains shaken, as the administrative machinery failed to reconcile its own signs, requiring external verification to correct a ledger error. The idea that India stands outside world history remains unshaken, as the day’s events were confined to the private and domestic management of a mistaken allotment.",
